{
"opening": "This release integrates several upstream improvements to enhance type safety, metric support, and formatting precision within the humanize library. It ensures that public APIs behave consistently with updated typing standards and new functional capabilities.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m27",
"text": "The functions Unit, activate, apnumber, clamp, deactivate, fractional, get_translation, intcomma, intword, naturaldate, naturalday, naturaldelta, naturalsize, naturaltime, ordinal, precisedelta, and scientific must be exposed at the top level of the package. These functions should operate according to their existing documented behaviors without regression."
},
{
"id": "m28",
"text": "The function metric must be exposed at the top level of the package and accept numeric inputs to return a string representation using SI unit prefixes. The function scientific must also remain available for returning numbers in scientific notation format."
},
{
"id": "m29",
"text": "The function intcomma must correctly handle the ndigits parameter when set to 0, ensuring that decimal places are stripped or formatted as specified without raising errors. It should return a string with thousands separators applied to the integer portion of the number."
},
{
"id": "m32",
"text": "The functions naturaldelta, naturalsize, and naturaltime must expose accurate type hints compatible with modern Python typing standards. Their runtime behavior regarding input types and output strings must remain unchanged from previous stable releases."
}
],
"closing": "Please verify that all listed public names are accessible via standard imports and that no deprecation warnings are introduced unexpectedly."
}
